  "coverage": [
    "All four shield types, three tiers and five sizes: 60 cases, rest/block/continued hold/return.",
    "All 21 weapon kinds: native compatibility and gauntlet independence; actual type changes while blocking, attacks, breakage, unequip, menus, compatible unarmed block/release.",
    "Real +zoom input toggles on/off, sustained hold, +attack native animation clock, +forward movement, boxed suppression and restoration.",
    "Three gauntlet tiers and five sizes: real +zoom guard/hold/release, broken-source suppression; save/load held T3 and release.",
    "Exact 960x720, 1280x720 and 1680x720 native screenshots; no crop/repaint applied to captures.",
    "Four old baseline shield saves (T2/M, each type), final build reload, re-save and reload: held pose and release, equipped identity/type/tier/size/durability/count preserved."
  ],
  "qualifications": [
    "Isolated test fixture creates native items and invokes native equipment actions. It bypasses character size restrictions to cover every sprite combination; the shield matrix refills Air. These are presentation tests, not balance changes or a normal campaign playthrough.",
    "Source-level protection confirms unchanged gameplay definitions. Air naturally decreases during held-block save tests; it is not expected byte-identical after advancing time.",
    "Save snapshots cover the equipped shield and reported inventory count, not every unrelated campaign quest. Old persistent state tables are byte-identical; added presentation caches are transient.",
    "Shield matrix/aspect captures use the shield_candidate package; those assets, native registration and shield controller bytes are unchanged in the final package. Final transitions, input, gauntlet and old-save checks use final_with_gauntlets.",
    "Saved QA counters are cumulative. passes_in_this_log counts only assertions actually executed in that process.",
    "Earlier local fixture mistakes (initial weapon raise wait, integer TEXTURES offsets, serialized cfg waits and save path handling) were corrected before passing runs. Intermediate logs remain in ignored build/issue106.",
    "No engine binary, IWAD, saves or QA fixture is shipped. Capture backgrounds come from the installed development IWAD and are test evidence, not runtime art.",
    "Initial narrow-guard screenshots and source hashes are historical. Revised guard/icon captures and package hash are in author_revision; gameplay and view state logic were unchanged by this art correction."
  ],
